            %em calibration
            of an oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+p-form"} differential p-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^p(X)
            with the property that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                it is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+differential+form"} closed
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi ω
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \omega = 0
            %li
              %p
                evaluated on any oriented
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
                for at least one choice of subspace.
          %p
            A Riemannian manifold equipped with such a calibration is also called a
            %em calibrated geometry
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82
            ) or similar.
          %p
            A
            %em calibrated submanifold
            of a manifold with calibration is an oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            such that restricted to each of its tangent spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %em equals
            the induced volume form of the submanifold there.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#minimal_volume_submanifolds Minimal volume submanifolds
          %p
            Any calibrated submanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \hookrightarrow X
            minimizes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            in its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            class.
          %p
            For Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \Sigma \hookrightarrow X
            be a homologous
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stokes+theorem"} Stokes theorem
            together with the condition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \phi = 0
            implies that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration of differential forms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            equals that over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inequality"} inequality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi vol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mi cal
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi subm
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mover
                    %mo =
                    %mi Stokes
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mover
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mover
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi calib
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mover
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mi d
                  %mi vol
                  %mo =
                  %mi vol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  vol(\Sigma)
                  \\stackrel{cal\,subm}{=}
                  \\int_\Sigma \phi
                  \\stackrel{Stokes}{=}
                  \\int_{\tilde \Sigma} \phi
                  \\stackrel{calib}{\leq}
                  \\int_{\tilde \Sigma} d vol
                  \=
                  vol(\tilde \Sigma)
                  \\,.
          %h3#CalibrationsFromSpinors Calibrations from spinors
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            For suitable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} spin representation
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            with its canonical Riemannian structure becomes
            = succeed "-calibrated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi ϵ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ¯
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi p
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega_{\epsilon}
                  \\coloneqq
                  (\overline{\epsilon} \Gamma_{a_1 a_2 \cdots a_p} \epsilon) \, e^{a_1} \wedge \cdots \wedge e^{a_p}
          %p where
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^a\}
                denotes the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+1-forms"} differential 1-forms
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
                is a non-vanishing
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor"} spinor
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo ¯
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mn 2
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mi p
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\epsilon} \Gamma_{a_1 a_2 \cdots a_p} \epsilon
                is the
                %a{:href => "spin+representation#SpinorBilinearForms"} canonical bilinear pairing
                which in components is given by evaluating
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+form"} quadratic form
                given by multiplying the skew-symmetrized product of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                of the representation matrices
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma^a
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+conjugation+matrix"} charge conjugation matrix
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DadokHarvey93"} Dadok-Harvey 93
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 7
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 3
            then this gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
            calibration.
          %p
            More generally for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariantly+constant+spinor"} covariantly constant spinor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
            gives a calibration.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The globalization of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-manifold"} G₂-manifold
                is a calibration. A calibrated submanifold in this case is also called an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+submanifold"} associative submanifold
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+4-form"} Cayley 4-form
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29-manifolds"} Spin(7)-manifolds
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original articles are
          %ul
            %li#HarveyLawson82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reese+Harvey"}> Reese Harvey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H.+Blaine+Lawson"} H. Blaine Lawson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calibrated geometries
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reese+Harvey"}> Reese Harvey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calibrated geometries
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathunion.org/ICM/ICM1983.1/Main/icm1983.1.0797.0808.ocr.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+spinors"} Killing spinors
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reese+Harvey"}> Reese Harvey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spinors and Calibrations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.elsevier.com/books/spinors-and-calibrations/harvey/978-0-12-329650-4"} publisher
            %li#DadokHarvey93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jiri+Dadok"}> Jiri Dadok
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reese+Harvey"} Reese Harvey
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calibrations and spinors
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calibrated_geometry"} Calibrated geometry
            %li
              %p
                Jason Dean Lotay,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calibrated submanifolds and the Exceptional geometries
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/joyce/theses/LotayDPhil.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#application_in_string_theory Application in string theory
          %p
            Discussion in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            includes the following.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"}> Gary Gibbons
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Papadopoulos"} George Papadopoulos
                %em Calibrations and Intersecting Branes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9803163"}> arXiv:hep-th/9803163
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jerome+Gauntlett"}> Jerome Gauntlett
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"} Neil Lambert
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+West"} Peter West
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Branes and Calibrated Geometries
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9803216"} arXiv:hep-th/9803216
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Papadopoulos"}> George Papadopoulos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Gutowski"} Jan Gutowski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em AdS Calibrations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9902034"} arXiv:hep-th/9902034
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Gutowski"}> Jan Gutowski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Papadopoulos"} George Papadopoulos
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and generalized calibrations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9905156"} arXiv:hep-th/9905156
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Gutowski"}> Jan Gutowski
                , S. Ivanov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Papadopoulos"} George Papadopoulos
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformations of generalized calibrations and compact non-Kahler manifolds with vanishing first Chern class
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0205012"} arXiv:0205012
